        {
          "id": 3336705110,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I was thinking after I've gone through the various checks a bit more I would want to use concurrent.futures.ProcessPoolExecutor (one future for each file checked) as I've done with the other scripts.\n\nUsing futures is probably worth it for when developers have \\> 1 file to check, but what effect would it have on pipeline time/costs?  Do they run with multiple cores available?",
